---
title: Sausage & sweet potato traybake
servings: 6
course: dinner
tags: baked, one-pan, pork, potato
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/10/Sausage-Sweet-Potato-Bake-eaa36e6.jpg?resize=900,836
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/sausage-sweet-potato-traybake
prep time: 15m
cook time: 45m
---

Heat the #oven{} to 200 C/180 C fan/gas 6 or if using the #air fryer{} heat to 200 C.

Mix together @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @paprika{2%tsp}, @fennel seed{2%tsp}, @dried oregano{2%tsp}, @barbecue sauce{2%tbsp} and @olive oil{2%tbsp}(or vegetable or rapeseed oil) in a #bowl{}.

Tip @red onion{2}(peeled and quartered), @corn cob{2}(cut into 4-6 pieces), @mango{1}(stoned and chopped), @sweet potato{2}(large, cut into wedges) and @pork sausage{8} into a #baking tray{}, then pour over the sauce and stir to coat. Season.

Bake in the #oven{} for ~{45%minutes}, giving it a toss halfway through, until the sausages are cooked through and the sweet potato is soft. If freezing, leave to cool completely first. Can be frozen for up to one month. Defrost thoroughly before reheating in the #oven{} at 200 C/180 C fan/gas 6 for ~{35%minutes}.

Serve sprinkled with @?coriander{}(chopped) and @?chilli{}(chopped), if you like.
